  "title": "Recognize ‘I Knew It All Along’ Thinking",
  "description": "When reviewing past events: - Ask yourself: \"Did I really know this beforehand, or is it hindsight talking?\" - Write down predictions: Track what you think will happen before events unfold. - Stay humble: Accept that outcomes often feel clearer after they’ve happened. Example: After a project fails, resist thinking, \"I knew this wouldn’t work.\" Reflect instead on what you actually knew at the time.",
